    "narrative": "The Austin Waves look primed for a high-ceiling performance today, headlined by the middle infield duo of **Gunnar Henderson** (83.29) and **Luis Garc\u00eda Jr.** (74.56). Both players benefit from ideal matchups against Will Warren and Chris Bassitt, respectively, with favorable park factors adding double-digit boosts to their daily efficiency scores. **Gunnar Henderson** stands out as the premier play; his combination of power and the expected advantage against Warren creates an elite profile that should anchor our production. Similarly, **Jackson Merrill** (73.27) and **Kyle Tucker** (73.93) provide stability in the outfield, with **Kyle Tucker** offering high-end consistency despite a slightly lower spot in the order, while **Andy Pages** (72.19) and **Heliot Ramos** (70.57) round out a strong offensive core that is well-positioned to capitalize on these matchups.\n\nWhile our lineup construction is aggressive, we are monitoring several \"Lineup Pending\" statuses that could introduce volatility. **Nasim Nunez** (55.84) and **Coby Mayo** (54.99) carry risk due to their lower projected order spots, though both maintain acceptable floors. The most difficult bench decision involved **Wade Meckler** (51.24), who missed the cut despite a favorable leadoff projection. Ultimately, the optimizer favored the higher raw power and secondary category potential of **Drake Baldwin** (58.62) and **Jacob Wilson** (58.75), as the Waves prioritize high-efficiency outcomes in a tight 5x5 race. We must remain vigilant regarding the confirmed lineups for **Liam Hicks** and **Jacob Wilson**, as any shifts in their batting order will necessitate an immediate review of their situational utility.\n\nFinally, while we are operating with a full, healthy roster, it is worth noting that **Vladimir Guerrero Jr.** remains sidelined on the IL, further necessitating that our available starters maintain this level of daily efficiency. With **Luis Robert Jr.**, **Jordan Westburg**, **Josh Jung**, and **Curtis Mead** currently out of the active rotation mix, our depth is being tested. We will continue to avoid underperforming assets like **Luis Lara** (38.35), whose matchup against Logan Gilbert presents a significant obstacle that the optimizer rightly identified as a \"Below floor\" scenario. Tonight\u2019s success rests on **Gunnar Henderson** and the top-tier outfielders maximizing their favorable park environments to secure those critical SB and R categories.",
